```rust
pub struct ModeResult {
  pub candidates: Vec<Candidate>,     // up to k, best score first
  pub pairwise_distance: Vec<Vec<f64>>, // variation-of-information matrix
  pub solution_space_converged: bool, // true when fewer than k survived
}
```
--{ ref: 0071de33-90ff-48a9-8e43-d65b2aa70a22 }--

{{ ref: 56225af9-10e4-492a-ae6a-012f041e0ef0 }}
- **Behaviour**: Every candidate carries a score breakdown (cut / imbalance / naming / path / anchor) and delta narration against the current tree, so users see *why* it ranks where it does. If the surviving pool collapses below k, fewer candidates are returned with `solutionSpaceConverged: true` — itself a meaningful signal that the solution space is tight. Identical snapshot + config + seed produces byte-identical candidates.
--{ ref: 56225af9-10e4-492a-ae6a-012f041e0ef0 }--
{{ ref: a569d431-dd6d-408c-a450-09c4ee606e16 }}
- **Compatibility**: First release. Scores are comparable only within one Strata version; `result.json` records its `schemaVersion`, and `InputUnreadable` rejects files from incompatible versions.
--{ ref: a569d431-dd6d-408c-a450-09c4ee606e16 }--